<title>FRANCE: Sommer-Allibert rises on unit sale plan.</title>
<headline>Sommer-Allibert rises on unit sale plan.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Sommer-Allibert rose strongly after the company said it was planning to sell its bath room activities.</p>
<p>&quot;The group is going to concentrate on its core activities. The deal will generate cash which they can use to develop their international activities. It's very good news,&quot; a dealer said.</p>
<p>At 1101 GMT, Sommer was up 3.8 percent at 166.10 francs after having hit a high at 174 francs.</p>
</text>
